    <statement><p>If <m>C</m> is the
part of the circle <m>\displaystyle \left( \frac{x}{5} \right)^2 + 
\left( \frac{y}{5} \right)^2 = 1</m> in the first
quadrant, find the following line integral with respect to arc length.</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle \int_C (2x-7y) ds =</m>
<fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2\cdot 5^{2}-7\cdot 5^{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
